 "brief_summary": "The primary objective of the study was to evaluate the effect of 12 weeks of subcutaneous evolocumab administered every 2 weeks and once a month, compared with placebo, on percent change from baseline in LDL-C when used in combination with statin therapy in adults with high cardiovascular risk and with hyperlipidemia or mixed dyslipidemia.",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria: Male or female, Japanese adult, 20-85 years of age; Subjects on stable dose of statin for greater than equal to 4 weeks; Fasting LDL-C greater than equal to 100 mg/dL; Fasting triglycerides less than equal to 400 mg/dL; Subject is at high risk for cardiovascular events. Exclusion Criteria: New York heart Association (NYHA) III or IV - heart failure; Uncontrolled cardiac arrhythmia; Uncontrolled hypertension; Type 1 diabetes, poorly controlled type 2 diabetes; Uncontrolled hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism",
  "sex": "ALL",
  "minimum_age": "20 Years",
  "maximum_age": "85 Years",
  "healthy_volunteers": false,
